     "claim": "K_hook",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "On 17 June 2019 at the Packer Marine Terminal, Port of Philadelphia, U.S. Customs and Border Protection with federal, state and local partners found cocaine worth more than $1 billion (CBP's estimate: about $1.3 billion street value) in seven shipping containers aboard the container ship MSC Gayane. Narration: 'Smugglers loaded a ship with a billion in cocaine.' Headline 'A BILLION-DOLLAR / COCAINE SHIP'. The shipping line was not accused of wrongdoing and is not named on screen.",
     "urls": [
      "https://cbp.gov/newsroom/local-media-release/us-customs-and-border-protection-seizes-msc-gayane-following-record",
      "https://maritime-executive.com/article/philadelphia-cocaine-bust-was-largest-in-cbp-s-history",
